1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:05,922
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:07,090
[indistinct chatter]

3
00:00:07,173 --> 00:00:10,135
[NARRATOR] <i>The epicenter of</i>
<i>what shook the markets that day</i>

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,303
<i>was the Bank of Japan,</i>

5
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:15,640
<i>commonly called the BOJ.</i>

6
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:17,392
IMPLEMENTATION OF ADDITIONAL
MONETARY EASING MEASURES

7
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:19,019
<i>Monetary easing.</i>

8
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,104
<i>In layman's terms,</i>

9
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:23,398
<i>a country increases the amount</i>
<i>of money in circulation...</i>

10
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:24,399
BOJ
BUYING GOVERNMENT BONDS, ETC.

11
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:25,400
CASH INJECTION
CORPORATIONS INDIVIDUAL

12
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:27,902
<i>...stimulating inflation while</i>
<i>depreciating currency value.</i>

13
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:31,156
<i>Setting aside</i>
<i>the policy's pros and cons,</i>

14
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:33,408
<i>this announcement</i>
<i>betrayed the expectations</i>

15
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:34,409
<i>of market traders</i>

16
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,662
<i>and came as a violent shock</i>
<i>to investors.</i>

17
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:39,330
[flames roaring]

18
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:41,624
<i>A giant blazing column emerged</i>

19
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,044
<i>in the USD/JPY market.</i>

20
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,716
[KURUMI] $1 equals ¥112?

21
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:50,717
[chuckles]

22
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,969
That's definitely one
for the history books.

23
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:56,514
-[mouse clicks]
-Hmm.

24
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,475
UNREALIZED GAIN/LOSS

25
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:00,435
It's a wild party,

26
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,437
but I doubt
it'll keep going for long.

27
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:05,482
Normally,
I'd want to lock in gains now.

28
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:07,567
[bubbling]

29
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:10,612
♪

30
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:13,323
<i>But this is different.</i>

31
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:19,245
The right thing this time
is to jump in.

32
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:21,831
Going full power long.

33
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:23,667
-Firing 120 lots!
-[clicks]

34
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:25,710
LONG POSITIONS
OPEN VOLUME

35
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:26,878
LIQUIDATE ALL LONG POSITIONS

36
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:30,674
<i>After taxes,</i>

37
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,426
<i>the amount I'm aiming for</i>
<i>is ¥20 million.</i>

38
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:34,511
BALANCE

39
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:36,179
<i>I'm still pretty far.</i>

40
00:01:36,262 --> 00:01:38,973
<i>But if a market boom</i>
<i>develops out of nowhere...</i>

41
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:42,519
<i>...and if I burn everything</i>
<i>on this long,</i>

42
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:44,688
<i>I can get close to it all</i>
<i>at once.</i>

43
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:49,984
[stifled laughter]

44
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:53,738
UNREALIZED GAIN/LOSS

45
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:57,283
<i>Oh, man, I can't stop laughing.</i>

46
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,493
[stifled laughter continues]

47
00:01:58,577 --> 00:02:02,914
KURUMI'S ROOM

48
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:05,834
[♪ opening theme song playing]

49
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:35,173
GLOBAL HOME DELIVERY

50
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:37,425
♪

51
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:40,720
[MEBUKI]
The food they sent from home.

52
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:42,180
It's here!

53
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:43,598
Just in time, too.

54
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,017
Ooh, yay!

55
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:47,018
TO MEBUKI
CURRY SPECIAL

56
00:03:47,102 --> 00:03:48,228
It's curry city up in here!

57
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:49,521
Uh?

58
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,524
[paper rustling]

59
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:53,525
WE SENT YOU SOME FOOD,
SO KEEP YOUR CHIN UP!

60
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,693
[MEBUKI'S MOM] <i>"Dear Mebuki,</i>

61
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:57,696
saving up
for school can't be easy.

62
00:03:58,571 --> 00:03:59,948
<i>We sent you some more food,</i>

63
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,992
<i>so try and keep a smile</i>
<i>on that pretty face.</i>

64
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,119
<i>Love, Mom."</i>

65
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:05,662
[whimpers]

66
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:07,747
[sighs softly]

67
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:09,708
-[message notification tone]
-Ah.

68
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:11,668
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE
FROM MOCHIKO-SENPAI.

69
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:12,752
It's from Mochiko?

70
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,629
What could it be?

71
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:16,297
USD/JPY IS CRAZY

72
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,675
[grunts in shock] <i>"Crazy"?</i>

73
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:22,637
<i>You must mean that in, like,</i>
<i>like, in a good way, right?</i>

74
00:04:25,432 --> 00:04:27,434
[whimpering]

75
00:04:28,852 --> 00:04:29,769
[gasps]

76
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:33,148
PRICE - TAKE PROFIT - STOP LOSS
PRICE - SYMBOL

77
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:38,361
NOTICE OF LOSS CUT EXECUTION

78
00:04:38,445 --> 00:04:39,654
[gasps in horror]

79
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:40,822
REGARDING LOSS CUT RULES

80
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:42,699
<i>Forced liquidation?</i>

81
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:46,953
[SHUDDERING]
<i>Oh, hell. This is so, so bad.</i>

82
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:49,372
<i>I'm in trouble</i>
<i>if I don't get that back.</i>

83
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,917
<i>I've gotta move money</i>
<i>into my forex account.</i>

84
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,753
<i>No, I can't.</i>

85
00:04:55,337 --> 00:04:56,588
ACCOUNT STATEMENT
BALANCE: 871 YEN

86
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:59,466
<i>I already put everything in,</i>
<i>so I'm broke.</i>

87
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:03,970
Oh, yeah,
how much is in my wallet?

88
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,472
Nothing!

89
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:06,806
It's empty!

90
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:08,725
Why's it empty?

91
00:05:08,808 --> 00:05:09,726
[exclaims]

92
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:12,729
These coupons aren't
worth anything to me!

93
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:13,730
[grunts]

94
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:16,983
I know! Magic deposit.

95
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:21,488
PLEASE SELECT A DEPOSIT METHOD.
CREDIT CARD

96
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:24,491
It's perfect!
Boy, am I a genius or what?

97
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,201
They're so pretty, too!

98
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:29,162
I had three of them issued
to get more bonus points.

99
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:31,664
I haven't been using these
at all lately to save money,

100
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,750
so I should be able
to max out all three.

101
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:36,711
Combined credit limit
of ¥300,000!

102
00:05:36,795 --> 00:05:38,254
I can keep fighting
with this much!

103
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:41,925
<i>And with credit cards,</i>
<i>I can pay in installments.</i>

104
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:44,511
Excuse me,
it's hard for me to get by.

105
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:45,512
REVO-KUN

106
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:46,596
That's not a problem.

107
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,015
You just need to pay ¥10,000
every month.

108
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:52,519
That'll make balancing
your budget super easy.

109
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:55,146
<i>I have a feeling</i>
<i>I can do revolving payments.</i>

110
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:58,274
<i>But... is that a good idea?</i>

111
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:00,777
[GULPS]
<i>When it comes down to it,</i>

112
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,779
<i>isn't this a little dangerous?</i>

113
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,700
Ah! I have to go short now.

114
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,577
Credit card ban, lifted!

115
00:06:09,661 --> 00:06:11,746
NAME PRINTED ON CARD:
MAKE DEPOSIT

116
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:12,956
YOUR DEPOSIT COMPLETED
SUCCESSFULLY - BALANCE

117
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,290
Immediate attack!

118
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:17,002
Short USD/JPY 20 lots!

119
00:06:17,669 --> 00:06:18,670
VOLUME EXECUTION PRICE
COMPLETED

120
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:21,256
Yes! I got in
right before the crash!

121
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:24,926
If it falls ¥10 yen from here,
I can earn ¥2 million!

122
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:25,927
YEN

123
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:27,512
I can get it all back at once!

124
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:31,766
<i>Forced liquidation</i>
<i>will be at ¥114,</i>

125
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:33,018
<i>one-and-a-half yen higher.</i>

126
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:36,271
<i>There's no way</i>
<i>it's going to climb any higher.</i>

127
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:37,480
Huh?

128
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:42,694
Why?

129
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,904
Why is it still going up?

130
00:06:47,991 --> 00:06:51,327
Oh, no,
it's trying to kill me again.

131
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:53,955
[whimpers] Mochiko, help.

132
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:55,373
What do I do?

133
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:58,793
Kurumi won trading AUD/JPY,

134
00:06:58,877 --> 00:07:01,463
and she had to borrow money
to do it.

135
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,925
Oh, yeah, she did let me in
on Kurumi's secret, huh?

136
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:09,471
As long as I have funds,
I won't be forced liquidated.

137
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:13,224
I just have to keep borrowing
until I win.

138
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:16,353
Even if I don't have money
on hand right away,

139
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,021
it doesn't mean
I should give up.

140
00:07:18,605 --> 00:07:21,524
Whenever the chance comes,
throw money at it and win.

141
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:24,277
[chuckles]
Seems like a pretty unbeatable

142
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:25,653
investing cheat to me.

143
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:26,946
-[YASUKO] Mebuki!
-Uh?

144
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:28,114
[gasps]

145
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,867
Yasuko, you're here?

146
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,952
♪

147
00:07:34,204 --> 00:07:36,539
Uh, maybe I'm getting
carried away.

148
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:38,792
Borrowing that much
wouldn't be a good idea.

149
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:41,044
I'd be in huge trouble
if I lost after that.

150
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:42,879
Well, that's a relief.

151
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,464
You came to your senses.

152
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:46,758
You can take a step back
for now.

153
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:48,426
-[whimpering]
-Uh?

154
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:51,012
I'm sorry.

155
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:54,391
Yasuko,
I don't think I can quit.

156
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,018
I lost money
I couldn't afford to lose.

157
00:07:57,102 --> 00:07:58,895
I even used credit cards.

158
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:00,438
I can't go back now. [sobs]

159
00:08:00,522 --> 00:08:01,898
I'm trapped.

160
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:03,149
I have to.

161
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:05,568
My only choice is to win!

162
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:07,404
[grunts]

163
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,034
[fire crackling]

164
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:17,706
[NARRATOR] <i>Each step you climb</i>
<i>on this staircase</i>

165
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:19,958
<i>scorches away</i>
<i>a little more of your life.</i>

166
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:22,585
<i>It could be a hellish spiral</i>

167
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:25,088
<i>that twirls you upwards</i>
<i>into infinity.</i>

168
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:27,090
<i>Knowing that...</i>

169
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:28,425
[sizzles]

170
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:31,928
<i>...Mebuki's only choice</i>
<i>was to climb it.</i>

171
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,973
<i>If only she could make it</i>
<i>to the top,</i>

172
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:38,059
<i>then she could recoup</i>
<i>all her losses to date.</i>

173
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:46,234
<i>Because the crash she hopes for</i>
<i>might be one step ahead.</i>

174
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,454
[MEBUKI] <i>Win and get it back.</i>

175
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,080
<i>I can still get it back.</i>

176
00:08:59,164 --> 00:09:00,707
<i>I need to get it back.</i>

177
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:05,462
<i>It'll be okay. I'm not afraid,</i>

178
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:08,798
<i>because Kurumi</i>
<i>was in the same position once.</i>

179
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:13,845
<i>It's a loan for justice,</i>
<i>then I can win at forex.</i>

180
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:14,846
CASH: AGE 18 AND OVER
SAME-DAY CASH - STUDENT LOANS

181
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:17,349
[WOMAN] <i>Are you having</i>
<i>trouble finding a job?</i>

182
00:09:17,432 --> 00:09:19,351
[MAN] <i>Pick some nice job-hunting</i>
<i>apparel and get 20% off.</i>

183
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:20,352
EMPLOYMENT & INTERNSHIP EVENT!!
SUITS LOOK GREAT TOO!

184
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:24,022
Ugh, I hate trying
to look for a job.

185
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:26,608
I wanna be a student
for a little longer.

186
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:27,609
EMPLOYMENT & INTERNSHIP EVENT!!
LIMITED TIME 15% OFF

187
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,027
[MOCHIKO]
Do you really need a job anyway?

188
00:09:29,611 --> 00:09:31,780
Can't you get by using forex?

189
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:32,947
[KURUMI] I don't know.

190
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:34,616
Being a full-time trader?

191
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,494
But is that an option?
[chuckles]

192
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:39,829
Huh? I was just joking.

193
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:41,664
Yeah, I was only kidding, too.

194
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:43,875
I plan on quitting forex
while I'm still ahead.

195
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:46,836
But anyway, have you heard
from Mebuki at all?

196
00:09:47,462 --> 00:09:48,380
[MOCHIKO] Hmm.

197
00:09:49,464 --> 00:09:51,174
Looks like she did text me.

198
00:09:51,257 --> 00:09:53,968
She says she's too busy
to make it over today.

199
00:09:54,052 --> 00:09:55,762
Well, that's a shame.

200
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:57,889
[MEBUKI] <i>"I can't make it today.</i>

201
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,516
<i>I ran out of money,</i>

202
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,267
<i>so I'm taking out</i>
<i>a student loan,</i>

203
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:03,895
<i>keeping up</i>
<i>my USD/JPY short battle.</i>

204
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:07,273
<i>We can stick it out together</i>
<i>through this climb."</i>

205
00:10:07,941 --> 00:10:10,360
[MOCHIKO] <i>So she hasn't lost</i>
<i>any motivation,</i>

206
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,904
<i>and she's even taking on</i>
<i>additional debt.</i>

207
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,906
ROGER THAT.

208
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:19,786
<i>Then I guess I'll stay long</i>
<i>on USD/JPY.</i>

209
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:21,788
AVERAGE RATE
VALUATION PROFIT/LOSS

210
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,289
-[YASUKO] It's no good!
-[BOTH] Huh?

211
00:10:23,373 --> 00:10:25,291
[YASUKO] The size is way off!

212
00:10:26,001 --> 00:10:29,254
What's the point in having me
try on clothes anyway?

213
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:30,880
I'm not looking for a job.

214
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:33,174
Yasuko, you look so cute.

215
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:34,843
I'd hire you right on site.

216
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:36,845
You're just doing this
so you can laugh at me!

217
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:37,846
They'd all be like,

218
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,097
-"Let's go get sushi!"
-[YASUKO] What's that

219
00:10:39,681 --> 00:10:40,807
-supposed to mean?
-[MOCHIKO] <i>She's so tiny.</i>

220
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:42,559
But one thing's true,

221
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:45,478
I know I can't just keep doing
part-time gigs forever.

222
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:47,689
2-BUTTON TAILORED JACKET
STRAIGHT SKIRT

223
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:52,110
You know how I said I draw manga
last time we were hanging out?

224
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:54,654
I've actually posted
a few panels since then.

225
00:10:55,155 --> 00:10:56,906
WHEEZE
DISQUALIFIED!! DO IT OVER

226
00:10:56,990 --> 00:11:00,076
MAYBE THE FULL MARATHON
DIDN'T WORK OUT...

227
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,661
BWUH - DON'T UNDERESTIMATE
LABOR EXPLOITATION!

228
00:11:01,745 --> 00:11:03,246
I'VE WORKED
AT THREE SUCH COMPANIES,

229
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:04,914
AND I THINK I KNOW
HOW TO DEPICT IT.

230
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:06,541
HUH? THEY'RE NOT
GROWING OUT...

231
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,834
I'M A CURSED RABBIT.

232
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:09,836
EVERY FIVE RETWEETS,
MY TEETH GROW LONGER.

233
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:11,921
Not a single joke
ended up landing.

234
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,798
-What? Not one?
-And guess

235
00:11:13,882 --> 00:11:15,842
which ended up
getting the biggest response.

236
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:16,843
YASUKO
ONE OF MY TOENAILS IS INGROWN...

237
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:18,887
This is just dumbass
everyday grumbling.

238
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:20,722
I don't need likes for this.

239
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:23,892
[MOCHIKO] Haven't you figured
out any strategies or trends?

240
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:25,810
[YASUKO]
Nope. I still have no idea

241
00:11:25,894 --> 00:11:27,228
what people think is funny.

242
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,023
-[grunts]
-[BOTH] Hmm?

243
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,525
This writer's callus
on my finger

244
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,402
is howling in sorrow.

245
00:11:34,486 --> 00:11:35,904
♪

246
00:11:41,493 --> 00:11:43,370
Truth is, I was naive.

247
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:44,371
CHANGE LOVE INTO INFLUENCE.
NOW'S YOUR CHANCE TO GO VIRAL.

248
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:47,207
[sighs] Now I'm out of ideas.

249
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:49,000
[MOCHIKO] Well,
have you tried this one yet?

250
00:11:49,084 --> 00:11:50,919
A manga where a rabbit
trades on forex.

251
00:11:51,002 --> 00:11:52,003
Huh?

252
00:11:52,087 --> 00:11:53,880
A little rabbit who does trades?

253
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:56,257
-[choral chanting]
<i>-What do I do?</i>

254
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:57,967
I lost it all.

255
00:11:58,051 --> 00:12:00,261
Using the forex marketplace
is brutal.

256
00:12:00,929 --> 00:12:02,722
A single dried plum to eat.

257
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:04,849
I wish I was dead.

258
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:07,727
[grunts]

259
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:10,605
I could never draw
something so pitiful!

260
00:12:10,689 --> 00:12:11,940
What are yo, a fiend?

261
00:12:12,023 --> 00:12:13,733
-No! No! No!
<i>-She's assuming it's gonna lose.</i>

262
00:12:14,359 --> 00:12:16,194
[sighs in exasperation]
I guess I'll just fall back

263
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:18,196
on the only thing
that's ever gotten a little--

264
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,197
Hold on.

265
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,740
12,000

266
00:12:20,824 --> 00:12:23,118
-I think I'm going viral.
-What?

267
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:24,661
Really? Let me see.

268
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:25,662
THE TALE OF A RABBIT
WHO CAN'T BEAT EARTH'S GRAVITY

269
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,789
[YASUKO] I kinda just
drew this manga on a whim.

270
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,040
[KURUMI EXCLAIMS] It's cute!

271
00:12:29,624 --> 00:12:32,002
-I like this one.
-You do?

272
00:12:32,085 --> 00:12:33,920
So if I put that character
in a book

273
00:12:34,004 --> 00:12:35,714
and slap it on some merch,

274
00:12:35,797 --> 00:12:37,757
maybe it would sell.

275
00:12:38,425 --> 00:12:40,552
Going viral isn't enough
to guarantee sales.

276
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:43,179
What? I think it would sell
if she put it out there.

277
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:45,974
You're always buying stuff
like this for yourself, Mochiko.

278
00:12:46,057 --> 00:12:47,517
Just look at it.

279
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:49,269
[exclaims softly]

280
00:12:49,811 --> 00:12:50,895
[YASUKO]
<i>I'm glad people like it,</i>

281
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:53,898
<i>but it kinda got mixed feelings,</i>
<i>if I'm being honest.</i>

282
00:12:53,982 --> 00:12:56,443
<i>I don't have a whole lot</i>
<i>of confidence in that thing.</i>

283
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:58,862
<i>Oh, but wait.</i>

284
00:12:59,988 --> 00:13:01,990
<i>When was the last time</i>
<i>I had any success</i>

285
00:13:02,073 --> 00:13:04,409
with a trade that I felt
really confident about?

286
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:05,785
[inaudible dialogue]

287
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:09,164
<i>My confidence isn't</i>
<i>what I should be trusting.</i>

288
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:10,832
<i>The fact is,</i>

289
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:14,044
<i>this manga got a response,</i>
<i>and I should be trusting that.</i>

290
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:15,920
All right!

291
00:13:16,004 --> 00:13:18,048
Everything in my forex account

292
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:20,425
is gonna be invested back
into my crappy manga!

293
00:13:21,092 --> 00:13:22,761
Even if it does end up flopping,

294
00:13:22,844 --> 00:13:25,263
it's better than
getting killed off on forex.

295
00:13:25,347 --> 00:13:27,432
[MOCHIKO] So you're going to
quit forex altogether?

296
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:28,725
[YASUKO] Sure am.

297
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:32,020
Wow! I'm impressed
you can stand by that decision

298
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:33,855
right when the market's
on the verge of blowing up.

299
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:36,191
Why? Is something big going on?

300
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:37,984
Yasuko,
you really haven't heard?

301
00:13:38,068 --> 00:13:40,153
The BOJ pulled the trigger
on additional easing,

302
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,782
which weakened the yen.
USD/JPY is at 113.

303
00:13:43,865 --> 00:13:44,866
[grunts]

304
00:13:46,117 --> 00:13:48,578
<i>Mebuki. Is she okay?</i>

305
00:13:49,204 --> 00:13:51,122
Kurumi has been
making a killing.

306
00:13:51,206 --> 00:13:53,375
-What are your unrealized gains?
-Eh?

307
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,002
[whimpers]

308
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,381
It's a secret.

309
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:01,424
[MOCHIKO] <i>That's irritating.</i>

310
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:04,260
Hey, when using foreign Forex,

311
00:14:04,344 --> 00:14:06,763
you can't go into debt
just from losing, right?

312
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:09,349
It's impossible to go into debt
from trading.

313
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:11,017
That's how the platform works.

314
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:15,355
But... it is possible
to put yourself into debt

315
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:16,815
just to keep trading.

316
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:17,816
[gasps]

317
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:19,859
[whimpers softly]

318
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:21,820
Guys, listen.

319
00:14:22,404 --> 00:14:23,655
Mebuki's in trouble.

320
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:26,408
She went short on USD/JPY
a while back,

321
00:14:26,491 --> 00:14:29,285
and now I'm worried she might
have lost it all somehow.

322
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,664
I kind of had my suspicions
about that.

323
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,959
<i>The first ¥200,000</i>
<i>she invested...</i>

324
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:36,960
VOLUME EXECUTION PRICE
COMPLETED

325
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,211
<i>...that had been turning</i>
<i>into a profit for her</i>

326
00:14:38,294 --> 00:14:40,922
<i>probably got wiped out by</i>
<i>this round of monetary easing.</i>

327
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:44,342
Yeah, that sounds like
it would track.

328
00:14:44,426 --> 00:14:45,802
[MOCHIKO] <i>I don't think it does.</i>

329
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:48,221
I really hope
this makes her give up

330
00:14:48,763 --> 00:14:51,516
and that she thinks of it
as an expensive life lesson.

331
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:54,310
But lately,
whenever I've seen her around...

332
00:15:00,191 --> 00:15:02,736
...I get this heavy
sinking feeling in my chest.

333
00:15:02,819 --> 00:15:04,571
Eventually, she's gonna mess up.

334
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:07,782
Look, there's gotta be something
we can do about this.

335
00:15:07,866 --> 00:15:08,783
Am I right?

336
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:10,952
-There's not.
-[exclaims in disbelief]

337
00:15:11,036 --> 00:15:13,038
Each of us is doing this
at our own risk.

338
00:15:13,121 --> 00:15:14,039
DERMATOLOGY CLINIC

339
00:15:14,122 --> 00:15:15,540
If Mebuki made this decision,

340
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,667
there's nothing we can do
that will save her.

341
00:15:19,127 --> 00:15:20,295
I AM SORRY THAT I BOTHERED YOU

342
00:15:23,298 --> 00:15:26,176
And beyond that,
none of this is our business.

343
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:27,177
[grunts]

344
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,928
But our friend
is in big trouble.

345
00:15:29,012 --> 00:15:30,638
Don't you think
you're being cold about this?

346
00:15:33,266 --> 00:15:35,852
Just for the record,
I'm also concerned.

347
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:37,771
Because...

348
00:15:37,854 --> 00:15:38,897
[siren wailing]

349
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:41,066
...my mom killed herself,

350
00:15:41,149 --> 00:15:44,110
and she did it because
of the money she lost on forex.

351
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:56,664
[siren fades]

352
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,962
[train chugging]

353
00:16:07,217 --> 00:16:08,134
SHINTO LOAN, INC.
ACCOUNT STATEMENT

354
00:16:08,218 --> 00:16:10,387
[MEBUKI]
<i>I went and borrowed 300,000 yen.</i>

355
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:12,847
<i>As long as I at least pay</i>
<i>the interest every month,</i>

356
00:16:12,931 --> 00:16:14,432
<i>there aren't any penalties.</i>

357
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:16,393
<i>It's more lenient</i>
<i>than I expected.</i>

358
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,521
<i>Now I should be able</i>
<i>to tough it out for a while.</i>

359
00:16:19,604 --> 00:16:21,773
BALANCE
POSITION

360
00:16:24,359 --> 00:16:26,945
Uh, uh, w-why?

361
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:29,155
None of this is right at all!

362
00:16:29,239 --> 00:16:30,323
This has to be wrong!

363
00:16:31,241 --> 00:16:32,867
This has to be bullshit!

364
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:35,954
PROFIT/LOSS

365
00:16:36,037 --> 00:16:39,457
<i>It's only been two days</i>
<i>since I made the last deposit.</i>

366
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:40,458
[grunts in frustration]

367
00:16:41,251 --> 00:16:42,877
[flames roaring]

368
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:49,300
<i>My ¥600,000 that I pulled</i>
<i>from out of bounds.</i>

369
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:53,221
[hyperventilating]

370
00:16:57,684 --> 00:16:59,978
[stifled retching]

371
00:17:04,149 --> 00:17:07,318
[retching, coughing]

372
00:17:10,572 --> 00:17:12,574
I thought I was invincible,

373
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:14,534
that I would never lose.

374
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:18,079
Just keep shouldering the burden
and then wait for the crash.

375
00:17:18,163 --> 00:17:19,998
There was no other way
for me to win.

376
00:17:20,623 --> 00:17:21,875
[cell phone buzzing]

377
00:17:23,043 --> 00:17:25,211
MEBUKI, YOU GOOD? LET'S GO
TO THE ARCADE, IT'S BEEN AGES!

378
00:17:25,295 --> 00:17:27,839
<i>Great, now she'll know</i>
<i>I read her message.</i>

379
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:29,841
I'LL PAY FOR BOTH OF US.

380
00:17:30,467 --> 00:17:33,345
A ¥300,000 deposit
won't get me anywhere.

381
00:17:33,428 --> 00:17:34,387
KURUMI-SENPAI
VOICE CALL

382
00:17:34,471 --> 00:17:36,639
I really didn't
wanna turn to her, but...

383
00:17:44,773 --> 00:17:45,690
Awesome!

384
00:17:45,774 --> 00:17:46,941
-[cell phone buzzing]
-Hmm?

385
00:17:47,025 --> 00:17:49,444
MEBUKI-CHAN
INCOMING CALL

386
00:17:49,527 --> 00:17:51,488
[ringtone playing]

387
00:17:51,571 --> 00:17:54,032
[KURUMI] <i>Hey, there!</i>
<i>It's been a while. What's up?</i>

388
00:17:55,116 --> 00:17:57,243
[MEBUKI] Hi, Kurumi. I'm sorry.

389
00:17:58,119 --> 00:18:00,705
I'm calling to ask you
to loan me money.

390
00:18:00,789 --> 00:18:02,957
[KURUMI]
Uh, that's kinda sudden.

391
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:06,002
<i>You running low?</i>
<i>How much money do you need?</i>

392
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:09,714
The amount I'm asking for
is about a million yen.

393
00:18:09,798 --> 00:18:11,174
Whoa, I see.

394
00:18:11,257 --> 00:18:13,051
You're asking for a lot of cash.

395
00:18:13,134 --> 00:18:15,470
So what would you be
using that money for?

396
00:18:15,553 --> 00:18:17,013
<i>I need to make sure I win.</i>

397
00:18:17,555 --> 00:18:19,599
You'd use it on forex, you mean?

398
00:18:19,683 --> 00:18:20,600
<i>Yes.</i>

399
00:18:21,226 --> 00:18:22,602
Listen, Mebuki,

400
00:18:23,311 --> 00:18:25,605
I know you're gonna regret this,
so please don't do it.

401
00:18:26,356 --> 00:18:27,857
<i>You should</i>
<i>pull out of the market,</i>

402
00:18:27,941 --> 00:18:29,818
<i>-accept defeat with some grace.</i>
-[gasps]

403
00:18:29,901 --> 00:18:30,985
BALANCE

404
00:18:31,069 --> 00:18:32,821
PROFIT/LOSS

405
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:34,197
[shrugs]

406
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:36,157
No, Kurumi.

407
00:18:36,783 --> 00:18:38,910
<i>If you were in the position</i>
<i>I am right now,</i>

408
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:40,412
<i>could you call it quits?</i>

409
00:18:40,495 --> 00:18:41,663
[flames roaring]

410
00:18:43,498 --> 00:18:44,666
Kurumi...

411
00:18:45,917 --> 00:18:47,210
...it'll be fine.

412
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:48,920
There's no way
I can keep losing.

413
00:18:49,671 --> 00:18:51,089
I need your help.

414
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:53,800
I could keep fighting
if I had a million yen.

415
00:18:53,883 --> 00:18:56,594
Oh, yeah, and this wouldn't be
for free, either.

416
00:18:58,388 --> 00:19:00,015
I'll pay you back the million.

417
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:01,725
I'll give you 100,000!

418
00:19:01,808 --> 00:19:05,228
That's a great deal for you,
right? Right?

419
00:19:05,311 --> 00:19:07,647
I promise
I'll get it back to you.

420
00:19:07,731 --> 00:19:09,733
Please help me.
You have to help me.

421
00:19:11,192 --> 00:19:12,110
Please.

422
00:19:14,529 --> 00:19:16,448
Help me, please.

423
00:19:25,165 --> 00:19:26,958
[KURUMI] I won't. I'm sorry.

424
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:29,210
[whimpers]

425
00:19:29,878 --> 00:19:31,379
[flames roaring]

426
00:19:32,756 --> 00:19:34,632
<i>Is that how little you trust me?</i>

427
00:19:34,716 --> 00:19:36,176
The reason why has nothing to do

428
00:19:36,259 --> 00:19:38,053
with whether or not I trust you.

429
00:19:38,136 --> 00:19:40,889
It's because you're losing,
and you keep losing.

430
00:19:41,473 --> 00:19:43,892
<i>I know someone</i>
<i>who literally died doing this!</i>

431
00:19:43,975 --> 00:19:44,893
[gsaps]

432
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:47,604
All right, Kurumi.

433
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:49,731
<i>This isn't convincing anyone.</i>

434
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:50,732
Uh!

435
00:19:51,358 --> 00:19:53,735
<i>You keep on telling me</i>
<i>I'm going to regret this,</i>

436
00:19:53,818 --> 00:19:55,528
<i>but will I, really?</i>

437
00:19:56,446 --> 00:19:59,032
You made mad gains
after you borrowed some money!

438
00:19:59,115 --> 00:20:00,784
<i>Aren't you glad</i>
<i>you took the risk</i>

439
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,410
<i>and did it in the end?</i>

440
00:20:02,494 --> 00:20:04,579
-Hold on a second.
<i>-Just forget it!</i>

441
00:20:04,662 --> 00:20:06,498
<i>I'm sorry I was unreasonable!</i>

442
00:20:06,581 --> 00:20:07,665
[line disconnects]

443
00:20:07,749 --> 00:20:08,667
[exclaims softly]

444
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,127
[sighs]

445
00:20:11,753 --> 00:20:12,962
[grunts]

446
00:20:14,798 --> 00:20:16,257
That freaking idiot!

447
00:20:16,341 --> 00:20:17,676
YASUKO-CHAN, I WANTED TO SHARE
THAT MEBUKI-CHAN CALLED ME

448
00:20:18,677 --> 00:20:21,179
Hey, get out here, Mebuki!

449
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:23,139
I know you're hiding out
in there!

450
00:20:26,768 --> 00:20:28,019
Is she in there?

451
00:20:28,687 --> 00:20:29,729
[EXCLAIMS] Oh, no.

452
00:20:31,314 --> 00:20:32,232
MEBUKI
VOICE CALL

453
00:20:32,315 --> 00:20:34,776
Please. Come on, girl,
I'm begging.

454
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:37,028
-You gotta answer!
-[line dialling]

455
00:20:37,112 --> 00:20:38,655
Uh, Mebuki,
where are you right--

456
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:39,656
-[line disconnects]
-Uh?

457
00:20:40,782 --> 00:20:42,075
Oh, great!

458
00:20:45,662 --> 00:20:47,122
[MOCHIKO] Hey, have you heard?

459
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:48,707
Kurumi was saying

460
00:20:49,332 --> 00:20:52,002
her mother lost at forex
and then committed suicide.

461
00:20:52,544 --> 00:20:53,878
I wonder if it's true.

462
00:20:54,629 --> 00:20:55,755
[meows]

463
00:20:57,841 --> 00:21:00,969
<i>But it's a bit abnormal</i>
<i>if it is. Think about it.</i>

464
00:21:01,678 --> 00:21:03,513
<i>How could she</i>
<i>have ever started forex</i>

465
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:05,348
<i>if someone in her family died?</i>

466
00:21:05,432 --> 00:21:07,142
-[doorbell ringing]
-Huh?

467
00:21:11,813 --> 00:21:13,523
<i>I guess</i>
<i>it's none of my business.</i>

468
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:18,153
Sorry to show up
all of a sudden.

469
00:21:19,279 --> 00:21:20,655
It's fine. Come on in.

470
00:21:21,197 --> 00:21:22,157
[grunts in hesitation]

471
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:28,163
So, what were you wanting
to discuss?

472
00:21:32,709 --> 00:21:34,794
I know this is a lot,
but I'm begging!

473
00:21:36,171 --> 00:21:38,506
Please, loan me some money.

474
00:21:40,050 --> 00:21:41,801
I'm struggling. [sobs]

475
